  "findings": [
    "At circle return, accepted edges 0->26 and 1->26 adjust translation by only 0.042 m and 0.013 m; measured constraint does not encode the approximately 1 m physical return correction.",
    "81-86% of selected planar correspondences at start/return are horizontal surfaces. Weak translation axis is nearly world Y, matching the endpoint-error direction. This is a point-to-plane normal-information proxy, not actual GICP covariance.",
    "Correspondence search is local (0.3 m); accepted overlap >=0.7 is insufficient evidence of accurate longitudinal registration in this geometry. These findings support geometric ambiguity/local-minimum diagnosis, not proof that every accepted edge is false.",
    "Increasing loop translation information by 100x barely improves circle return and still worsens slope endpoint separation relative to no loops. Blind weight increase is not a fix.",
    "Accumulated frontend error remains before graph optimization; the cause of all frontend drift (kinematics vs LiDAR/IMU) has not been isolated here.",
    "Two independent raw no-loop replays of circle produce the same 0.0333 m native frontend return, versus 1.0279 m live frontend. Loop closure cannot account for this frontend discrepancy; actual accepted live input sequence was not traced on that run. Do not attribute all live drift to geometric ambiguity or claim 3 cm live accuracy."
  ],
